{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779842443,"nonce":"eNzKndYbJ+R9tKTgx+8Fm67Oc54=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDeuu_Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/183","origin":"github"},"title":"Operator awareness of active collision avoidance — CAMP map overlay + annunciator","message":"## Motivation\n\nReflex collision avoidance is now live and was validated on-water on 2026-05-26 (rolker/unh_echoboats_project11#173) — but the operator has **no indication** of when it is acting or what it sees. A student operator can't tell the boat slowed/stopped *because of CA* vs. some other reason. We need CA state surfaced in the operator UI.\n\n## Two parts\n\n**1. CAMP map overlay** (camp) — draw, on the map:\n- the reflex obstacle cloud `/bizzy/collision_monitor/pointcloud` (what CA sees),\n- the slowdown (0–20 m) and stop (0–5 m) polygons `/bizzy/collision_monitor/{slowdown,stop}_polygon`,\n- the gating state `/bizzy/collision_monitor_state` (NONE / SLOWDOWN / STOP), e.g. polygon color change on action.\n\nSo the operator sees both what CA perceives and when it intervenes, georeferenced on the map.\n\n**2. Annunciator row** that lights (WARN/active) when the Collision Monitor is in SLOWDOWN or STOP.\n- Note: `collision_monitor_state` is `nav2_msgs/CollisionMonitorState`, **not** a `/diagnostics` status — so this needs either a small adapter publishing a `DiagnosticStatus` from it, or a topic-source annunciator row. (Annunciator config lives in `bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat_operator_annunciator.yaml`.)\n\n## Dependencies / relations\n\n- Reliable bridged delivery of these perception topics → rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#127 (operator-side perception display over the bridge).\n- Surfaced on deployment #173 (CA validated on-water; the only operator feedback today was the boat's behavior itself).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}